> =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 A garden variety unmapped address follows the TSB miss=
 path, and when
> =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 no valid mapping is found in the process page tables, =
the miss=20
> handler
> =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 checks to see if the access was via a no-fault ASI.=C2=
=A0 It then fixes up
> =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 the target register with a zero, and skips the no-faul=
t load
> =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 instruction.
>
> =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 But different paths are taken for data access exceptio=
ns and=20
> alignment
> =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 traps, and these do not respect the no-fault ASI. We a=
dd checks in
> =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 these paths for the no-fault ASI, and fix up the targe=
